sc-range-start
    If the response included a Content-Range header (i.e., a partial/range request, common for video/large file streaming), this gives the byte range start.
    Justification: our main app doesn't require this, however we may want to investigate adding it in the future
    Verdict:

sc-range-end
    If the response included a Content-Range header (i.e., a partial/range request, common for video/large file streaming), this gives the byte range end.
    Justification: our main app doesn't require this, however we may want to investigate adding it in the future
    Verdict:

x-edge-response-result-type
    Similar to x-edge-result-type, but reflects the result type actually sent to the viewer, which can differ from x-edge-result-type in edge cases
    Justification: very similar to the other field but occasionally at edge results differ, this is more of a debug field than something to analyse. 
    AO's view: I believe it is worth keeping. A simple pie chart showing the distribution of errors, hits, misses, redirects and influence intuition when performing diagnostic work.
    Verdict:

x-edge-detailed-result-type
    When the result type is an error, this gives the specific error type — more granular than just "Error," useful for diagnosing what actually went wrong.
    Justification: used for diagnosing errors for analysis this isn't required.
    AO's view: I believe it is worth keeping. A simple pie chart showing the distribution of errors, hits, misses, redirects and influence intuition when performing diagnostic work.
